  "overallSourceFitness": "Oxygen cost of walking and running: the metabolic equations of the American College of Sports Medicine. Effort read from the heart rate reserve: Swain and Leutholtz, 1997. Comparison table: FRIEND (Kaminsky and colleagues, 2015), built from people in the United States who chose to take a treadmill test.",
  "overallOursFitness": "The ceiling at that position and the weight of {points} points.",
  "@overallOursFitness": {"placeholders": {"points": {"type": "String"}}},
  "overallLimitsFitness": "It comes from outdoor runs and walks recorded here with GPS and the ring, on stretches of 10 minutes or more without a pause. The ground is treated as flat, so hills make it read low. A maximum heart rate guessed from age can be off by 10 beats or more, and that moves the result. Without sex and an age from 20 to 79 in your profile, this row stays outside the count. The app never estimates fitness from the resting heart rate alone: that would count one measure twice.",
  "overallWhatResting": "How many times the heart beats a minute at full rest. The ring uses the calmest stretch of each night.",
  "overallRuleResting": "{zero} or more is worth zero, {full} or less is worth everything, and in between it is proportional.",
  "@overallRuleResting": {"placeholders": {"zero": {"type": "String"}, "full": {"type": "String"}}},
  "overallSourceResting": "The range: Quer and colleagues, 2020, with adults who wore a wristband day to day.",
