  "effortFormulaIntro": "Effort has four parts: points, strength days, load and the coach card. Every rule and every constant is on this screen.",
  "effortFormulaPointsTitle": "Effort Points",
  "effortFormulaPointsBody": "One point is one minute of moderate effort, and one minute of vigorous effort is {weight} points. In a recorded workout, heart rate is moderate from {moderate} percent of your max heart rate and vigorous from {vigorous} percent. By type, a workout under {moderateMet} MET earns nothing, from {moderateMet} MET it earns 1 point a minute and from {vigorousMet} MET it earns {weight}. The larger of the two counts. An imported workout counts by type only. Outside workouts, only walking at {cadence} steps a minute or more counts, at 1 point a minute.",
  "@effortFormulaPointsBody": {"placeholders": {"weight": {"type": "String"}, "moderate": {"type": "String"}, "vigorous": {"type": "String"}, "moderateMet": {"type": "String"}, "vigorousMet": {"type": "String"}, "cadence": {"type": "String"}}},
  "effortFormulaPointsNote": "Your max heart rate is the one you entered. Without one it is 220 minus your age, which can be off by 10 bpm or more for one person. With neither, heart rate is not used and the type of workout decides.",
  "effortFormulaWeekTitle": "The week",
  "effortFormulaWeekBody": "Monday to Sunday. Two targets of the same standing: {points} points and {days} strength days. A strength day has a strength training workout of {minutes} minutes or more. Past {points} points nothing more is asked.",
  "@effortFormulaWeekBody": {"placeholders": {"points": {"type": "String"}, "days": {"type": "String"}, "minutes": {"type": "String"}}},
  "effortFormulaLoadTitle": "Session load",
  "effortFormulaLoadBody": "One number for how much a session asked of you, with no unit. With heart rate it is the minutes in each zone times the number of the zone, from 1 to 5. The zones start at {zones} percent of your max heart rate. When you rate a session from 1 to 10, the minutes times the rating divided by {divisor} is a second figure, and the larger of the two counts. With neither it is the minutes times a default for the type of workout:",
  "@effortFormulaLoadBody": {"placeholders": {"zones": {"type": "String"}, "divisor": {"type": "String"}}},
  "effortFormulaLinesTitle": "Daily load and the two lines",
  "effortFormulaLinesBody": "The load of a day is the load of its sessions plus {walking} times the minutes of brisk walking outside workouts. Each line takes a share of the newest day and keeps the rest of itself: {acuteShare} for the {acute} day line and {chronicShare} for the {chronic} day line. Both start as the mean of the first {seed} days, run up to yesterday and show from {min} days of history.",
  "@effortFormulaLinesBody": {"placeholders": {"walking": {"type": "String"}, "acute": {"type": "String"}, "acuteShare": {"type": "String"}, "chronic": {"type": "String"}, "chronicShare": {"type": "String"}, "seed": {"type": "String"}, "min": {"type": "String"}}},
