  "aiGuideTitle": "Connect a model",
  "aiGuideLead": "Four steps. It takes about five minutes, and none of your data leaves the phone during setup.",
  "aiGuideStep1Title": "Choose a service",
  "aiGuideStep1Body": "It can be a service on the internet, paid per use, or a model running on your computer on the same Wi-Fi. OpenRing has no AI of its own and earns nothing from your choice.",
  "aiGuideStep2Title": "Create a key just for OpenRing",
  "aiGuideStep2Body": "On the service's site, under API keys, create a new key and set a monthly spending limit. If something goes wrong, the loss stops at that limit. Copy the key: it is shown only once.",
  "aiGuideStep3Title": "Paste the address, the model and the key",
  "aiGuideStep3Body": "Pick the service in the list to fill in the address. The model is the exact name the service uses, and the list button next to it shows the names the service offers.",
  "aiGuideStep4Title": "Test the connection",
  "aiGuideStep4Body": "The test sends a fixed sentence and none of your data. If something fails, the screen says what happened and what to do.",
  "aiGuideLocalTitle": "Model on your computer",
  "aiGuideLocalBody": "Ollama or LM Studio, with no key and no cost per use. The computer stays on and on the same Wi-Fi as the phone. In Ollama, allow connections from the network, not only from localhost, and set the context to 8192 tokens or more. The address is the computer on the network, for example http://192.168.1.10:11434/v1. This connection is not encrypted, so use it only on a network you trust. The key is optional and can stay empty.",
  "aiGuideCost": "What it costs depends on the service and the model. Each reading shows its tokens and, when the service reports it, the cost. The app has no price table, because prices change often.",
  "aiGuideOpen": "Open the connection",
